# New Feature Workflow

## New page template

1. Create `{name}-page.php` with `Template Name:` header
2. `get_header()` → `<main id="primary">` → sections → `get_footer()`
3. Register in README.md
4. Add body class filter in `functions.php` if needed

## New section template part

1. Create `template-parts/{area}/section-{name}.php`
2. Define `$defaults` array + `wp_parse_args()` merge
3. Add component CSS to `common.css` (`.hotw-{section}`)
4. Add responsive tweaks to existing `@media` blocks in `responsive.css`
5. Load via `get_template_part()` from page template

## New custom post type

1. Create `inc/post-type-{slug}.php`
2. `require_once` from `functions.php`
3. Prefix functions `hotw_register_{slug}_post_type`
4. Flush rewrites on `after_switch_theme`
5. Add single/archive templates when UI is needed

## New CSS

1. Tokens first in `variables.css`
2. Component rules in `common.css`
3. Breakpoints only in `responsive.css`

## New JavaScript

1. Add `initHotw{Feature}()` to `main.js`
2. Call from `DOMContentLoaded`
3. Guard selectors and library availability

## New images

Place in `assets/images/` with semantic names. Reference via `get_template_directory_uri()`.

## Before finishing

- Escape all output
- Use `heros-on-the-water` text domain for translatable strings
- No debug code, console.log, or hardcoded localhost URLs
- Update README if structure changes
